    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "b72004c6f0f2d7c540f70b92f5edcbedda7d3c9e16cab993bb341fb1d1ddf2c3",
      "text": "Day 7 · After breakfast, a day on Lake Titicaca, at about 3,810 m, the subject of many legends: dozens of floating reed islands, the Uros Islands, are home to islanders who live from fishing, tourism and crafts, weaving baskets, furniture and even boats, on which you can ride around the lake. Continue to Taquile Island, whose weaving was proclaimed a Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity by UNESCO in 2005. Lunch on the island and return to Puno.",
